    "result": "I've successfully fixed the tax rounding issue in the invoicing system. \n\n## Problem Summary\nThe issue was that tax calculations were using Python's default \"banker's rounding\" (round half to even) instead of \"round half up\" behavior. This caused tax amounts like 12.5 cents to round down to 12 instead of up to 13, which was incorrect for the invoicing system.\n\n## Solution Implemented\nI modified the `round_half_up` function in `/tmp/cc-fix-rounding-17vvg_2t/repo/invoicing/money.py` to properly implement \"round half up\" behavior where values exactly at the halfway point round away from zero.\n\n## Verification Results\n- \u2705 The specific failing test `test_reduced_rate_on_250_cents_rounds_up` now passes\n- \u2705 All 85 tests in the test suite now pass\n- \u2705 The example case works correctly: 5% on $2.50 now correctly returns $0.13 instead of $0.12\n\nThe fix ensures proper tax rounding behavior for the invoicing system while maintaining all existing functionality.",
